WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.912
Priya: Okay, keep the old endpoint for tomorrow. We agreed on twenty-four hours of coverage.

2
00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:15.288
Hannah: Does that include certificates and backend access? An idle endpoint can still lose readiness.

3
00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:22.680
Raj: Yes, those dependencies stay active too. Synthetic checks continue without customer traffic.

4
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:29.496
Lukas: Who checks the saved rollback route overnight? Don't rely on yesterday's successful validation.

5
00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:35.544
Anika: I'll keep an eye on business checks. Raj owns both pools' network readiness.

6
00:00:35.544 --> 00:00:42.840
Priya: Just to confirm, no automatic deletion, right? Removing it needs a separate action item.

7
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:50.112
Hannah: Correct, and record the escalation path. Who can authorize a return overnight?

8
00:00:50.112 --> 00:00:55.872
Raj: The change on-call can authorize that. I can restore the previous weights.

9
00:00:55.872 --> 00:01:02.016
Lukas: Only after checking the old pool's health. Returning to an unhealthy pool adds risk.

10
00:01:02.016 --> 00:01:09.000
Priya: Agreed, that's roughly our overnight safety net. So, document it before the handoff.

